{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nA `docker compose` recreate driven by autodeploy left `compose-review-bot-1` in a **zombie** state: uvicorn began a graceful shutdown, **closed its listening socket**, and then never completed shutdown or exited. The container stayed `Up`, the queue worker kept running long agentic LLM reviews and casting votes, but nothing was listening on :8000 — so every request to `https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/review/` returned **502**, and, more damagingly, **every Gerrit webhook delivery was refused**.\n\nLive production outage 2026-08-28 23:21:37 UTC -> 23:43:31 UTC (~22 min).\n\n## Proven root cause (with citations)\n\n**1. It is a dead listener, not a slow one, and not a lost port mapping.**\n\nThe port publish was intact throughout — `docker ps`: `compose-review-bot-1 | Up 2 hours | 127.0.0.1:8000->8000/tcp`, and host `ss -ltnp` showed `docker-proxy` LISTEN on `127.0.0.1:8000`. But **inside** the container `/proc/net/tcp` held only:\n\n```\n0: 0B00007F:8EAD ... 0A     <- 127.0.0.11 (Docker embedded DNS), the ONLY listener\n1: 020015AC:8C6C ... 01     <- ESTABLISHED outbound to :443 (worker calling Bedrock)\n```\n\nPort 8000 (`0x1F40`) was **absent**. Host probe: `curl 127.0.0.1:8000/health` -> `curl: (56) Recv failure: Connection reset by peer`, `code=000`, `total=0.004s`. nginx logged `recv() failed (104: Connection reset by peer) while reading response header from upstream` 45 times — a **502, never a 504**. docker-proxy accepted the TCP connection and got RST because nothing was bound inside.\n\n**2. The mechanism is an incomplete uvicorn graceful shutdown.**\n\n```\n2026-08-28T23:21:37.438Z  compose creates replacement container 62f25f31ae05 + SIGTERMs the old one\n2026-08-28T23:21:37.587Z  INFO:     Shutting down\n2026-08-28T23:21:37.687Z  INFO:     Waiting for application shutdown.     <- listener socket closed HERE\n2026-08-28T23:21:52     first 502 in nginx access log (15s later)\n```\n\nThere is **no** matching `Application shutdown complete` / `Finished server process` anywhere in the log, and no second `Application startup complete` (only the original at 22:01:45). `docker inspect` confirms `RestartCount=0`, `Started=22:01:39`. uvicorn closes the listening socket at the *start* of graceful shutdown, then awaits lifespan shutdown — which never returned, because in-flight review tasks kept running. Evidence the process stayed fully alive with the listener shut: `voter_voted` at 23:35:12 and an agentic LLM call at 23:39:23, ~18 minutes after the listener closed.\n\n**3. The recreate then deadlocked on the port.**\n\n`docker rm`'d container `62f25f31ae05` was `State=created`, `Created=2026-08-28T23:21:37.438Z`, no ports — it could never start because the zombie still held `127.0.0.1:8000`. Compose gave up, leaving a half-finished recreate.\n\n## Impact: review dispatch WAS stalled, and events were dropped\n\nGerrit delivers webhooks **container-to-container** (`http://review-bot:8000/webhook`), not through nginx — which is why the nginx access log contains zero `POST /review/` entries and the 502 alone understates the damage. Gerrit's `webhooks` plugin logged, repeatedly, from 23:21:37 onward:\n\n```\nERROR com.googlesource.gerrit.plugins.webhooks.PostTask : Failed to post: Processing event: comment-added\norg.apache.http.conn.HttpHostConnectException: Connect to review-bot:8000 [review-bot/172.21.0.2] failed: Connection refused\n```\n\nBoth intake paths were dead simultaneously:\n- **webhook intake** — refused (listener closed).\n- **reconcile backstop** — `{\"event\": \"reconcile_loop_stopped\", \"timestamp\": 1787959359.86}` at 23:22:39. The same lifespan shutdown that closed the listener also stopped the reconciler; it was the one shutdown task that *did* complete.\n\nPer ADR 0009 the webhooks plugin is **not** at-least-once, so events in that window were **dropped, not retried**. The worker was only draining the finite in-memory queue captured before 23:21:37.\n\n## Remediation performed (surface restored)\n\n```\ndocker rm 62f25f31ae05          # inert Created leftover, no ports, never started\ndocker restart d76f4a3e9106     # identical image 4c18557db1ec; NOT a redeploy/rebuild/config change\n```\n\nVerified: in-container `/proc/net/tcp` now shows `00000000:1F40 ... 0A` (0.0.0.0:8000 LISTEN); host `/health` -> `200 {\"status\":\"ok\",\"in_flight\":1,\"queue_depth\":0}`; `gerrit->bot code=200`; external `https://.../review/health` -> `200` on three consecutive probes. The reconcile loop immediately re-picked the dropped work (`merge_detection` at 23:43:32).\n\n## Note: this is NOT the MCP event-loop-blocking bug (dewy-rotatable-tarsier / change 2345)\n\nThat hypothesis was tested and **refuted**. Loop-blocking predicts intermittent recovery between reviews and a burst of backlogged `/health` responses; observed instead was a hard RST with **no listening socket at all**, persistently across quiet moments, for 22 minutes. Decisive counter-evidence after the restart: `/health` returns `200` in milliseconds **while `in_flight: 1`** — a review in progress does not block the HTTP surface in this service.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A `docker compose` recreate of `review-bot` cannot leave a container that has closed its listener but not exited: shutdown either completes within the stop timeout or the process is forced down, so the port is released for the replacement. **Done (change 2381, merge a36c7407):** the lifespan arms a daemon deadline that `os._exit`s the process when an orphaned `asyncio.to_thread` offload survives the bounded cancel; worst-case drain(1200)+cancel(10)+grace(90)=1300s < `stop_grace_period` 1320s, so the controlled exit fires before Docker's SIGKILL and the port is released.\n- [x] In-flight review tasks are cancelled (or awaited under a bounded deadline) during lifespan shutdown rather than blocking it indefinitely. **Done:** the pre-existing bounded cancel (`shutdown_cancel_seconds()`) unwinds the coroutines, and the new process-level force-exit bounds the OS-thread tail that the asyncio await cannot.\n- [x] The reconcile loop is not stopped while the process continues serving/working — or, if shutdown has begun, the process reliably terminates so a fresh container restores both intake paths. **Done (second clause):** the fix makes the process reliably terminate within the stop budget, so a fresh container restores both the webhook and the reconcile/backfill intake paths.\n- [x] A health/liveness signal distinguishes \"listener closed, process alive\" from healthy, so this state alarms instead of presenting as a silent 502. **Done (change 2384, MERGED):** added a per-container `healthcheck:` to the `review-bot` service in `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` (previously only `mcp` had one, so nothing at the container layer distinguished the zombie from healthy — the root of the \"silent\" 502). The probe hits the process's OWN listener over container loopback at `http://127.0.0.1:8000/health`; in the zombie state uvicorn has closed that listener, so the connection is refused, the probe exits non-zero, and after `retries` the container flips to **unhealthy** — an observable, alarmable signal instead of a container that reads green while serving nothing. It is reporting-only (autodeploy.sh runs `docker compose up -d` without `--wait` and gates on its own curl probe; `restart: unless-stopped` does not act on health), so it does not change the recreate contract. Regression test `test_reviewbot_healthcheck_probes_its_own_listener` asserts the stanza exists and probes the bot's own listener (mutation-checked: wrong port, wrong path, and removed-stanza all caught). The merged force-exit fix (change 2381) additionally bounds how long that unhealthy-zombie state can persist.\n- [x] Regression test: a SIGTERM delivered while a long review is in flight results in process exit (not an indefinitely-hung shutdown) within the compose stop timeout. **Done:** `test_shutdown_forces_process_exit_when_an_orphaned_to_thread_review_outlives_cancel` drives a real orphaned `asyncio.to_thread` at shutdown and asserts the force-down fires; `test_force_exit_deadline_stays_within_the_stop_grace_band` pins drain+cancel+grace < `stop_grace_period`; `test_clean_shutdown_with_no_orphaned_offload_does_not_force_process_exit` guards the clean-teardown half. Mutation-checked (3 mutants caught)."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788031555801279539,"uuid":"08b3db91-5cca-48f4-a33f-7132d1554637"}